  "notes": "In response to his partner's overcall, West leads the ♠Q against 3NT. This lead has guaranteed a spade stopper for South.\n\nThere are still only 7 top tricks (1 spade, 4 diamonds, and 2 clubs). South will have to knock out the ♥A to come to 9 tricks.\n\nIf East has the ♥A (as is likely from his overcall), South's only hope for the contract is that West began with a singleton ♠Q.\n\nSouth must duck the opening lead in dummy. If East overtakes with the ♠A, the ♠K and the ♠J both will be stoppers.\n\nIf East ducks, West will remain on lead, hopefully with no spades left to play. When East eventually wins the ♥A, South will still have a spade stopper.\n\nIf West has the ♥A and a singleton ♠Q, the duck cannot cost.\n\nIf West has the ♥A and a doubleton ♠Q, it is again necessary to duck at trick 1. If the ♠K is played from dummy, East will duck in the above layout. When West wins the ♥A, he will have another spade to play to East. By ducking at trick 1, South will be able to exhaust West's spades before the ♥A is knocked out.",
